WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Fatigue and failure. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Compare cyclic and one-time loading

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Repeated stress can initiate fatigue damage even when a single load is below a one-time strength limit. Cycles and material details matter.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: A component seeing 10,000 moderate cycles is a different case from one seeing a single static load; actual life needs tested data.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Failure case diagnosis

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Compare cyclic and one-time loading
